SHOPGRAPH — STAGE 7 "REFINE JSON FILE" + DIRECT DATABASEBUILDER INTEGRATION

GOAL

Extend the existing ShopGraph OCR Acquisition Pipeline with a new seventh
stage:

    7. Refine Json File

The OCR Acquisition Pipeline sub-task menu must become:

1. Reliable Receipt Detection / Crop
2. Perspective Correction
3. Receipt Size Normalization
4. Generate OCR Image Variants
5. Run Multi-Variant / Multi-PSM OCR
6. Compare OCR Results / Build Raw OCR JSON
7. Refine Json File
0. Return to Capability Sub Tasks

The complete:

    1. OCR Acquisition Pipeline

capability must automatically execute all seven stages in order.

IMPORTANT:

Stage 7 is NOT merely an optional export.

Its refined JSON output must plug directly into the existing DataBaseBuilder
workflow and become the preferred source for DataBaseBuilder's initial field
guesses.

The intended flow is:

    Receipt Image
        ↓
    OCR Stages 1-6
        ↓
    data/raw_ocr/<receipt>_raw_ocr.json
        ↓
    Stage 7 — Refine Json File
        ↓
    data/refined_json/<receipt>_refined.json
        ↓
    DataBaseBuilder
        ↓
    user review / correction
        ↓
    shopgraph_purchase_history.xlsx

Keep the existing menu flow and terminal UI style as close to the attached
codebase as possible.


============================================================
PART 1 — STAGE 7 OUTPUT
============================================================

Stage 7 reads:

    data/raw_ocr/<receipt>_raw_ocr.json

and creates:

    data/refined_json/<receipt>_refined.json

Do NOT overwrite the raw OCR JSON.

Process EVERY Stage-6 line.

Every object such as:

    "line_number": 1

must have exactly one corresponding refined line.

Do not discard:

    headers
    addresses
    payment lines
    totals
    weight lines
    garbage OCR
    metadata
    unknown lines

If a field does not apply, use:

    "NA"

Never omit required fields.


============================================================
REFINED LINE SCHEMA
============================================================

Every line must use this stable structure:

{
  "line_number": 1,
  "source_text": "ALDI",
  "classification": "store_name",
  "confidence": 0.99,

  "fields": {
    "Total": "NA",
    "Store": "Aldi",
    "Six-Digit SKU": "NA",
    "Product": "ALDI",
    "Tax Code": "NA",
    "Store Number": "NA",
    "Common Name": "NA",
    "Category": "NA",
    "Date 1": "NA",
    "Price 1": "NA"
  },

  "field_confidence": {
    "Total": 0.0,
    "Store": 0.99,
    "Six-Digit SKU": 0.0,
    "Product": 0.95,
    "Tax Code": 0.0,
    "Store Number": 0.0,
    "Common Name": 0.0,
    "Category": 0.0,
    "Date 1": 0.0,
    "Price 1": 0.0
  },

  "reasoning": {
    "Total": "Not a purchase item.",
    "Store": "Line identifies Aldi.",
    "Six-Digit SKU": "No merchandise SKU on this line.",
    "Product": "Best line-level interpretation preserves the OCR text.",
    "Tax Code": "No tax code.",
    "Store Number": "No store number on this line.",
    "Common Name": "Not applicable.",
    "Category": "Not applicable.",
    "Date 1": "No date on this line.",
    "Price 1": "No product price on this line."
  }
}

IMPORTANT CHANGE FROM THE EARLIER SPECIFICATION:

The "Product" field should contain the BEST GUESS for the line, even if the
line is not ultimately a merchandise item.

This is intentional because DataBaseBuilder presents every OCR line for human
review.

For example:

Input:

    ALDI

should normally produce:

    Product = "ALDI"

rather than:

    Product = "NA"

Input:

    Store #160

may produce:

    Product = "Store #160"

unless there is a more meaningful field-specific interpretation.

Input:

    SUBTOTAL 106.81

may produce:

    Product = "SUBTOTAL"

or another conservative cleaned representation.

The objective is:

    Give the human reviewer the best editable starting guess for each line.

Do not deliberately erase useful source text merely because the line is not
a purchase item.

However, do NOT manufacture product identities.

The Product field should be a clean best guess based on the line itself.


============================================================
WHY PRODUCT IS POPULATED FOR NON-PURCHASE LINES
============================================================

DataBaseBuilder currently reviews lines individually.

When the reviewer chooses:

    2. Correct Columns

the existing guess should be editable directly.

Therefore a source line such as:

    ALDI

should result in:

    Current Product: ALDI

    Enter corrected Product: ALDI

NOT:

    Current Product: NA

    Enter corrected Product: NA

The reviewer may then:

    press Enter to keep ALDI
    edit ALDI
    replace ALDI
    later choose Skip Line

Stage 7 therefore provides a BEST GUESS, not merely final database-worthy
purchase fields.


